id: pm-github-iswq
title: Use canonical unbounded pm list reads with the 2026.8.20 host contract
description: "pm-github already fail-closes complete-corpus receipts, but its production argv and user-facing diagnostics still use the deprecated list-all alias and its declared pm CLI/SDK floors predate 2026.8.20."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agents,cli-ux,complete-corpus,latest-cli,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-20T21:28:31.109Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T21:45:25.861Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T21:40:41.284Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T21:40:41.284Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Create failing exact-argv and alias-free real installed-CLI tests first; replace only the deprecated invocation and terminology; retain strict full unbounded fail-closed receipt validation; use top-level TypeScript imports and no any/dynamic imports; pin dev CLI/SDK and set peer/manifest floors to 2026.8.20; run release:check, exact measured-source coverage, pm health, reconcile, validate, npm/bun packed acceptance, dependency/vulnerability/privacy checks; document exact evidence and link the package PR plus companion item pm-cli-website-cbyb; do not merge or publish while pm-github-zqad or pm-github-v2kt blocks release"
risk: medium
confidence: 95
reporter: codex
severity: medium
repro_steps: "Run the production completePmListArgs vector with pm CLI 2026.8.20 and inspect stderr; scan index.ts, README.md, and complete-corpus tests for list-all."
resolution: "Migrated the existing strict whole-corpus reader to canonical pm CLI 2026.8.20 argv without weakening its completeness decoder, added exact and real packed acceptance, aligned compatibility declarations, updated terminology, and preserved separate privacy, release-order, and exact-coverage blockers."
expected_result: "Production invokes explicit unbounded canonical pm list --all --json with full/body/strict receipts; no alias deprecation reaches stderr; source, tests, docs, generated output, package dependency, peer floor, and manifest floor agree on pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.20."
actual_result: "Implemented canonical host-owned --pm-path plus --output-include full, unbounded amount/cost, then list --all --json --include-body --strict-read; all production errors/docs and direct test fixtures use canonical terminology. Pinned local CLI/SDK 2026.8.20, set peer and manifest floors to 2026.8.20, and removed the ignored manifest pm.compatibility envelope. TDD failed 2/6 before source edits, then passed 6/6. Full suite passed 261 tests. Current measured-source coverage passed at 92.40% lines, 82.58% branches, 91.75% functions across index.ts/projects.ts; this is not 100/100/100/100 and remains independently open as pm-github-9cjx. Docstring gate documented 92 declarations; production audit found 0 vulnerabilities; pack dry-run contained 13 intended files. Clean packed npm and Bun clients each read two open/closed items with items.length=count=total, no truncation/pagination/list-all receipt, and empty child stderr. A packed npm extension authenticated through gh, validated public repo access HTTP 200, and a retry dry-ran a real GitHub import against unbraind/pm-github with no writes and a complete empty tracker; one earlier pm-changelog import attempt timed out at 30 seconds and was not counted as a pass. pm CLI receipt issue #1070 records canonical --output-include full being misreported as legacy --full. Delivery is complete but merge/publication remain blocked by pm-github-zqad and pm-github-v2kt."
affected_version: pm-github 2026.8.18 with pm CLI 2026.8.20
component: whole-tracker pm CLI integration
customer_impact: Deprecated diagnostics can pollute machine stderr and stale compatibility floors allow hosts that do not provide the canonical contract this package now requires.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
