notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T21:33:00.194Z",codex,"2026-08-20 TDD: before the source edit, node --test test/complete-corpus.test.ts failed 2 of 6 tests because completePmListArgs still emitted --path/list-all and the real CLI wrote the deprecation diagnostic to stderr. After canonical argv, the stale local 2026.8.15 runtime rejected list --all as ambiguous while the host 2026.8.20 runtime passed; npm install updated the exact local @unbrained/pm-cli pin to 2026.8.20 and all 6 tests passed. Full npm test then passed 261 tests. Canonical --output-include full is currently misreported as legacy --full in the receipt, tracked upstream as pm-cli #1070; the acceptance rejects only actual list-all use until that CLI bug is fixed."
  "2026-08-20T21:44:42.154Z",codex,"2026-08-20 final gates before review: npm run release:check passed 261 tests and the current 92.40/82.58/91.75 three-metric measured-source gate, 92 documented declarations, zero production audit vulnerabilities, clean 13-file pack, and current changelog. pm health --strict-exit passed with three provenance advisories; pm merge reconcile --dry-run found 82 clean streams and no pending decisions; pm validate remained structurally valid with pre-existing legacy metadata/resolution/file warnings; duplicates reported one pre-existing closed exact-title cluster. GitHub Dependabot and secret-scanning open alerts were empty; code-scanning has no analysis, and Trivy is not installed, so neither is represented as green. Public pm-changelog 2026.8.17 first refused a bounded 5-of-82 read; explicit unbounded pm-arg controls restored all 289 changelog lines. The tool still invokes its deprecated internal alias until privacy-gated pm-changelog PR #148 can merge and release. Historical privacy/identity findings remain open under pm-github-zqad and publication order remains open under pm-github-v2kt."
